@startuml
' Workflow of the two skills. Render with:  puml assets/workflow.puml
' Kept next to the generated workflow.svg so the diagram stays revisable.
' NOTE: do not name the diagram (@startuml <name>): PlantUML would then write
' <name>.svg instead of workflow.svg, and the puml wrapper reports FAILED.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #666666
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #666666
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFDF0
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C9C29A
skinparam PartitionBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam TitleFontSize 15

title Two skills, one engine: where a PDF and a Markdown note each go

|#EDF3FB|pdf-to-obsidian   (input: a PDF)|
start
:parse - MinerU 4.x
PDF -> middle_json.json + images;
:md / normalize - structure, cross-reference links, figure crops
-> blocks.jsonl + meta.json;
:meta - your Zotero library, else arXiv / Crossref
-> the note's properties;
if (translation endpoint configured?) then (yes)
  :translate - reads each block's own flags
-> zh / caption_zh written back into blocks.jsonl;
else (no, or --no-translate)
  :translation skipped
this is the PDF -> Markdown-only mode;
endif
:render - blocks.jsonl -> note.md;
:verify - structural checks, exits 1 on broken output;
stop

|#F4F1FB|translate-markdown   (input: an English .md note)|
start
:md2blocks - segment the note by Markdown syntax
-> blocks.jsonl;
:translate - reads each block's own flags
-> zh / caption_zh written back into blocks.jsonl;
:render - blocks.jsonl -> note.md;
:verify - structural checks, exits 1 on broken output;
stop

legend right
  Both lanes write the **same intermediate**: blocks.jsonl, a list of typed
  blocks. What gets translated is decided there, by each block's own
  **translatable** flag - set by the segmenter that produced the block:
  MinerU's block types on the PDF side, Markdown syntax on the note side.
  That is why translating a PDF's note through its work directory
  (--stage translate, then --stage render) keeps the finer typing, while
  re-segmenting a finished note does not.
endlegend
@enduml
